    # v390 (2026-10-07) -- THE FOUNDATION: the superposition is the passage (the AGAPE clause). The operator's quotations VERBATIM in Portuguese (checked against the
    # texts embedded by sha256), translations OUTSIDE the quotes; numbers and statuses READ from the record fundacao_v390; the closure is LOGICAL; the programme stays OPEN.
    _fd390 = core.get("fundacao_v390") or {}
    _cl390 = _fd390.get("clausulas") or []
    _bo390 = _fd390.get("borchers") or {}
    _vb390 = _fd390.get("verbatim") or {}

    def _tx390(x_):
        t_ = str(x_)
        for a_, b_ in (("\\", r"\textbackslash{}"), ("_", r"\_"), ("%", r"\%"), ("&", r"\&"), ("#", r"\#"), ("$", r"\$"), ("{", r"\{"), ("}", r"\}"), ("~", r"\~{}"), ("^", r"\^{}")):
            t_ = t_.replace(a_, b_)
        return t_

    def _i390(x_):
        return str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _tk390 = lambda x_: r"\texttt{" + _tx390(x_).replace(r"\_", r"\_\allowbreak{}") + "}"
    _sh390 = ", ".join(_tk390(str((v_ or {}).get("sha256") or "")[:16] or "ABSENT") for v_ in _vb390.values()) or _tk390("ABSENT")
    s.append(r"\section*{The Foundation: the superposition is the passage (the Agape clause)}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The Foundation: the superposition is the passage (the Agape clause)}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{In this run the record did NOT seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if _fd390.get("all_verified") is not True else r"")
             + r"\textbf{The operator's word.} On 2026-10-07 the operator wrote that what was missing to close um.py was "
             r"``definir a superposição como a passagem do global lift que é o único teorema faltando'' (\emph{to define the superposition as the passage of the global lift, which is the only missing theorem}) … "
             r"``não existe acima, o piso limita, tentar estar acima é cair sem fim, infinitamente'' (\emph{there is no above, the floor bounds, trying to be above is falling without end, infinitely}). And ratified: "
             r"``esse é o fecho sim, o sistema continua aberto mas fechado logicamente'' (\emph{this is the closure indeed, the system stays open but logically closed}) … "
             r"``A cláusula se chamará “ágape” e a pedra se chamará “fundação”'' (\emph{the clause will be called Agape and the stone Foundation}). "
             r"To the name of the bottomless fall, the \emph{abismo} (abyss), and to the correspondence proposed by the management, the operator answered: ``Perfeito, concordo com tudo. Magnífico'' (\emph{perfect, I agree with everything; magnificent}; what «everything» refers to is stated by the management \textsf{[DECLARADO]}). "
             r"The three texts are embedded in the program by sha256 (" + _sh390 + r"); the file on disk is informative only. In the code the names carry no accent "
             r"(\texttt{Fundacao}, \texttt{agape}): a Lean identifier admits no accent, and the door's ruler asks for a fixed name.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The closure, in three pieces.} (1) The operator's \emph{definition}: the GLOBAL\_LIFT, the old Lemma 3 --- the program's only open remainder ---, \emph{is} the superposition: "
             r"what wanted to be above and bears no positive post \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}. (2) The \emph{refusal}, proved in the kernel: the stone \texttt{TGLExt.Fundacao} ("
             + _i390(_fd390.get("kernel_flags_ok")) + r" of " + _i390(_fd390.get("kernel_flags_total")) + r" declarations within the axiom trio) and the clause \texttt{agape}, the composition of the six "
             r"below, with a concrete model ($\mathbb{R}$, $\tau=\mathrm{id}$, $\theta_s(x)=e^{-s}x$, the One posited) showing the conjunction is not vacuous (\texttt{agape\_is\_inhabited}). "
             r"(3) The local \emph{passage}: the post lives in the passage (\texttt{the\_post\_lives\_in\_the\_passage}, on the finite face: the lift is unconditional on the internalised flow), "
             r"and the field law as a local law of horizon equilibrium at each point is known (Jacobson 1995 \textsf{[KNOWN]}), with hypothesis H3 named. "
             r"The closure is \emph{logical}; the programme stays \emph{open}; the gate does not move. In the Tetelestai check: the refusal is CLOSED (a kernel term), the passage is LINKED and KNOWN BY REFERENCE, "
             r"the definition is the operator's act.")
    _rows390 = []
    for c_ in _cl390:
        _rows390.append(r"(%s) & %s & %s (%s) \\" % (("i", "ii", "iii", "iv", "v", "vi", "vii", "viii", "ix")[min(int(c_.get("n", 1)) - 1, 8)], _tx390(c_.get("in_words") or "").replace("ω", r"$\omega$").replace("ε", r"$\varepsilon$"),
                                                       _tk390(str(c_.get("teorema") or "").replace("TGLExt.Fundacao.", "")), "in the kernel" if c_.get("no_kernel") else r"\textbf{NOT read in this run}"))
    s.append(r"\begin{center}\small\begin{tabular}{p{0.05\linewidth}p{0.5\linewidth}p{0.36\linewidth}}\hline & the clause, in words & the theorem \\ \hline "
             + (" ".join(_rows390) if _rows390 else r"& \text{n/a} & \\") + r" \hline\end{tabular}\end{center}")
    s.append(r"\textbf{A reading \textsf{[ONTO]} by the management: the Foundation and the abyss.} \emph{Foundation} comes from \emph{fundus}, the bottom; the \emph{abyss} (Gk. \emph{ábyssos}, bottomless) "
             r"is the fall without a bottom, face to face with it. Agape is defined, in 1 Cor 13, largely by negations: \emph{is not puffed up} (Gk. \emph{ou physioûtai}) and \emph{love never fails} "
             r"(Gk. \emph{oudépote píptei}, never falls); Rom 8:39, \emph{neither height, nor depth}; Eph 3:17, \emph{rooted and grounded in love}; 1 Cor 3:11, "
             r"\emph{no one can lay any foundation other than the one already laid}. The operator approved the correspondence; the status is \textsf{[ONTO]}: it carries no status to the theorem.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{What is not claimed.} Takesaki's dual scaling law ($\tau\circ\theta_s=e^{-s}\tau$) enters as \emph{data} \textsf{[KNOWN]}: its realisation on the core of a genuine type "
             r"$\mathrm{III}_1$ factor is not a term of this kernel. The stone does not prove the field equation in curved spacetime by a kernel term: it refuses the post above and puts the post in the passage. "
             r"It is not a proof of global existence; it does not declare quantum gravity confirmed; \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED} is never confirmation.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The precision of the Hamiltonian.} The operator wrote ``neste caso não, porque o hamiktoniano é a energia'' [sic] (\emph{not in this case, because the Hamiltonian is the energy}). "
             r"The operator bounded below is the \emph{energy} --- the generator of translations, with positive spectrum; the modular generator of a type $\mathrm{III}_1$ factor has \emph{no} floor (its spectrum is $\mathbb{R}$). "
             r"The bridge between the two is Borchers' form, already in the kernel (\texttt{ContratoQGv31.positiveEnergy\_orientation}, the bound on the upper half-plane; \texttt{halfsided\_inclusion}, under the AQFT witness; \texttt{ContratoH2.contract\_borchers\_form}, under contract H2, a named hypothesis"
             + (r" --- within the axiom trio in this run" if _bo390.get("ok") is True else r" --- \textbf{not read in this run}") + r"). "
             r"\textbf{A note by the management \textsf{[KNOWN]}, on the operator's machine.} The endless engine of this reading is not the forbidden perpetual motion of the first kind (energy from nothing) "
             r"nor of the second (work from a single heat source): a flow conserves its own generator, and the KMS state is invariant under its own modular flow. The house's dephasing law has Milburn's "
             r"form (in this paper), and Milburn's equation conserves energy exactly --- what is paid is coherence (entropy rises), not energy; that is why the engine delivers no work. The name the literature gives to such a machine, without energy dissipation and delivering no work, is \emph{perpetual motion of the third kind}.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Beside.} In the code-closure ledger, in what remains named of the closure and in the seals of the runtime of the One, the old text (the GLOBAL\_LIFT as the single open one) stays, "
             r"and the v390 reading enters beside it. The v388 record read a live memory file by sha (the seal chain appends to it): the disk reading is now declared outside every verdict, "
             r"and the copy of the pinned state (the backup taken before the v388 chain) is now checked by sha, as informative --- an erratum beside the conferidor amendment of 06/10. Part C now counts " + str(_ledger_counts_v389()[0]) + r" unique ledger paths (+1, the Foundation stone); the v389 section reads the v389 state (" + str(_ledger_counts_v389(ate=389)[0]) + r"), as it was sealed. Record: " + _tk390(_fd390.get("verdict") or "ABSENT") + r".")
